hat  here before you might have said don't go  into the woods or don't walk alone at  night that was just general advice for  staying safe but when I see what's  happening now it's different but are  people really less safe statistically no  say the police the number of violent  crimes against women has been falling  for years but people's perception of  safety on the city streets at night has  changed of course we feel differently  now about safety in our group of friends  we've all decided that we won't go out  alone anymore only in a group before  especially in summer you'd be out and  about go to a bar or a party somewhere  wander around the city we don't do that  anymore there's a growing sense of fear  throughout Freiburg Ali wants to take a  stand against this for three days he's  been calling on refugees to attend the  memorial  Fryeburg for the murdered student maria  it's the first time he's ever done  anything like this he was deeply shocked  that the suspect was an Afghan national  no I mean by doing this today we're  trying to show that we're not evil  people there are good and bad people  everywhere  maybe the young Afghan who allegedly  committed the crime has problems within  himself the most killer shot see there's  my name informs Romero another I don't  know much about him but not all Afghans  are like him how missing he's chosen  some flowers for the event  here in the center of freiburg ali is  getting nervous  how many people will turn up it's still  early luckily he says a refugee aid  worker is helping him Ali is just 22  years old and he doesn't have much  experience with this kind of thing but  it seems the three days of preparation  have paid off  burnham are avid in body care era when I  heard about what happened I felt really  really sick I felt so sick and went to  the hospital and they gave me some  medicine but I still didn't feel any  better and the stress wouldn't go away  that's why I wanted to do this to come  here with my friends and other people  who share my feelings  it's my calmness with Baker the refugees  are worried about how the attitude  toward them is changing could this  incident in Fryeburg hurt their chances  of staying in Germany almost all asylum  applications from Afghans are rejected  I'd like to thank everyone for coming  you all know why we're gathered here  today we're all deeply saddened by this  terrible tragedy with this event today  we want to show that there are good  Afghans to someone probably a troubled  and stupid individual did something bad  but we're not all like this I wish the  German government could see us as we are  here today  two weeks after the police arrested the  suspect local Afghans held up banners  denouncing the violent crime against the  young student Maria and the people of  Freiburg also took part  but there's a I never thought so many  people would come or so many different  people it's really surprised me in a  positive way the murder in Freiburg has  served only to bolster the populist sand  other opponents of refugees in Germany  after the memorial service more details  came to light about the suspects  criminal past in Greece in 2013 he  attacked a woman and pushed her over an  8 meter high embankment  she suffered serious injuries but  survived  Ali hopes that his involvement will help  to keep Freiburg a tolerant City a place  where refugees from Afghanistan feel  welcome  you

